---
import ProsePage from '../../templates/ProsePage.astro';
import ContactForm from '../../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { routePath } from '../../i18n/routes.ts';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, PRETALX_CFP_URL, REPO_URL, editionName } from '../../config/site.ts';

const edition = editionName('001');
---

<ProsePage
  locale="en"
  routeKey="contribute"
  title="Contribute"
  description="Four routes: a story on stage, a room, a field note, or an event you know about. None of them costs money."
>
  <p>
    This community is made of whatever people put into it. Below are the four routes that exist
    today, and exactly what each one asks for. Not sure which is yours? Mail
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> — one sentence is plenty.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell people something at {edition}</h2>
  <p>
    The evening opens with two twelve-minute field reports: one concrete thing you built, fixed or
    broke, and what you took away from it. No deck full of logos, no product pitch, no "the future
    of". Speaking experience is not required — a real story about a real system is the only
    criterion, and we will help you shape it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Twelve minutes, plus questions. Dutch or English, either is fine.</li>
    <li>The subject does not matter as long as you did the work yourself.</li>
    <li>Who gets on stage is decided by the open call, on the same terms for everyone.</li>
  </ul>
  {
    PRETALX_CFP_URL ? (
      <p>
        <a class="button button--primary" href={PRETALX_CFP_URL} rel="noopener">
          Submit your talk
        </a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        The open call currently runs by e-mail: send three sentences on what it is about to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Open%20call%20${edition}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If
        there are more proposals than slots, the call moves to a public submission tool with
        availability and review — it is ready, and it opens when it adds something.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Offer a room</h2>
  <p>
    An edition needs space for forty people, with food and drinks. That is the most valuable thing a
    company can contribute and the first thing we ask for — in-kind support always comes before
    money here. What you get for it, and what you explicitly do not buy, is on
    <a href={routePath('companies', 'en')}>companies</a>.
  </p>
  <ContactForm
    id="host"
    to={CONTACT_EMAIL}
    subject="Offering a room for a twente.dev edition"
    submitLabel="Send"
    fallbackLabel="Mail us"
    note="Sending opens your own mail app with this message in it — nothing goes to an external service."
    fields={[
      { name: 'org', label: 'Organisation', required: true },
      { name: 'contact', label: 'Name and e-mail address', required: true },
      { name: 'city', label: 'Town in Twente', required: true },
      { name: 'capacity', label: 'How many people fit, seated?', required: true },
      {
        name: 'offer',
        label: 'What can you offer — room, food, both, something else?',
        type: 'textarea',
        required: true,
      },
      { name: 'when', label: 'Which months would suit you?', type: 'textarea' },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Write a field note</h2>
  <p>
    The weekly field note is one concrete lesson from a local system, written by someone who works
    on it. Four to eight hundred words is enough. You do not have to be a blogger, and it does not
    have to be finished when you propose it — we edit alongside you, and your name goes on it. After
    that it lives in the <a href={routePath('blog', 'en')}>archive</a>, so it stays findable.
  </p>
  <ContactForm
    id="fieldnote"
    to={CONTACT_EMAIL}
    subject="Proposing a field note"
    submitLabel="Send"
    fallbackLabel="Mail us"
    note="Sending opens your own mail app with this message in it — nothing goes to an external service."
    fields={[
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name and e-mail address', required: true },
      { name: 'subject', label: 'What is it about?', required: true },
      {
        name: 'lesson',
        label: 'What is the lesson? One or two sentences is enough',
        type: 'textarea',
        required: true,
      },
      { name: 'language', label: 'Dutch or English?' },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>List an event or a community</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on this site is a file in a public repository, so a submission is an issue or a pull
    request. Pick whichever you find easier:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>An event</strong> — open to the public and relevant to developers.
      <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new/choose`}>Open the form</a>, or add the file yourself. It
      appears in the calendar and the ICS feed straight away.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A community</strong> — Discord, Slack, user group or meetup. We do not list anyone without
      asking, so preferably submit your own group;
      <a href={routePath('communities', 'en')}>the directory</a> explains how that works.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Found something broken or wrong? <a href={REPO_URL}>Open an issue</a>. The full step-by-step is
    in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/src/branch/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Supporting us</h2>
  <p>
    There is deliberately no donate button here. What we need is a room, food, people who turn up
    and someone willing to tell a story — all of which can be offered above. If an organisation
    wants to back an edition financially, that is a conversation rather than a rate card: mail
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. A payment route arrives only once there
    is something to fund that cannot be given in kind, and it arrives with a public account of it.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
